       "text": "**No, it is not safe to exercise outdoors in Jurong right now.** \n\nSingapore is experiencing severe transboundary haze, and the West region (which includes Jurong) is the hardest-hit area on the island. \n\nAccording to the latest readings from the National Environment Agency (NEA):\n* **24-hour PSI (West):** **212** — This falls into the **\"Very Unhealthy\"** range (201–300).\n* **1-hour PM2.5 (West):** **185 µg/m³** — This is in **Band 3 (High)** (151–250 µg/m³).\n\n### Official NEA Health Advisory for Current Readings:\n* **Healthy Individuals:** **Avoid** prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion. \n* **Vulnerable Persons** (elderly, pregnant women, children, and those with chronic lung or heart conditions): **Avoid all** outdoor activity. \n\n**Recommendation:** Move your workout indoors to an air-conditioned room or gym (ideally with an air purifier running), and keep windows and doors closed until the haze subsides. If you must go outside for essential errands, consider wearing an N95 mask to reduce your exposure to fine particulate matter.",
